From 4cad1285fb97b087a5bf83c9f358983b29d7b9fa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Luis Chamberlain <mcgrof@do-not-panic.com>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 12:40:40 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Add a headless --rl bridge for reinforcement learning

Run the race physics without a window, GL context or audio device so
an external learner can reset and step the game faster than real
time. "etr --rl" reads one request per line on stdin (info, reset,
step, quit) and answers one JSON object per line on stdout; the
banner and every other message the game prints go to stderr.

The step path feeds the same steering flip-flops the keyboard and
joystick handlers set and then calls the unchanged CalcSteeringControls
and CControl::UpdatePlayerPos, so a headless tick runs exactly the
rendered game code minus drawing. Reset replays CLoading, CIntro (the
start keyframe included) and CRacing::Enter at a fixed step, seeds
the C library RNG, and restores every collectable item.

Two static-initialisation hazards had to move: sf::RenderWindow and
sf::Texture are GlResources, and merely constructing one opens the
display, which SFML 3 turns into abort() when there is none. The
window and each TTexture now hold a lazily created pointer, and the
desktop-mode and joystick queries move from the CWinsys constructor
into Init(), which the headless mode never calls. TTexture::Load is a
no-op in headless mode. CControl gains a tree-contact event counter
so a learner can see collisions.

Signed-off-by: Luis Chamberlain <mcgrof@do-not-panic.com>
